menu "Haro Config"

    config HARO_DEFAULT_SERVER_URL
        string "Default Haro server WebSocket URL"
        default "ws://10.0.0.126:8765"
        help
            Compile-time fallback server URL, used by
            haro_config_get_server_url() only when NVS has no "server_url"
            value yet (e.g. a factory-fresh device that has never had
            haro_config_set_server_url() called on it -- nothing in the
            current boot path calls it; see main.c and Task 3's
            haro_config component).

            Without this fallback, a factory-fresh device's NVS read
            returns ESP_ERR_NVS_NOT_FOUND, which previously propagated to
            an ESP_ERROR_CHECK() abort in app_main() -- a permanent
            boot crash-loop, since CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_PANIC_PRINT_REBOOT
            reboots with no delay.

            This is a stopgap, not a substitute for real provisioning:
            override this value for your deployment before flashing
            production devices, or write the real URL to NVS (e.g. via
            esp_prov.py's custom-data mechanism, once a task wires that
            up) as soon as the device is provisioned.

endmenu
